;; The race (issue #17, clojure -M:race): every runner carries servers on one of the race's
;; pregenerated landing sets, each server its own race process and bots, each bot from a landing
;; of its own to the target. The other runners play the sim race (ci/simrace.edn).
;;
;; Sized by the capacity ramp of run 38348283421 (b2f34ea): with the bot's CPU cut to a third
;; (memo/by, path/cells), the slowest tenth of the bots held 20 ticks a second at every load up to
;; 210 bots a runner, so the bots are not the limit. A vanilla server ticks on one thread: its p95
;; tick was 67 ms at 30 bots and about 130 ms from 50. Two servers of 25 bots a runner ran at 130 ms
;; a tick, 7 to 8 ticks a second, in the rounds of 2026-10-15, and the bots' clock-against-ticks
;; rules paid for it (#88, #131, #199): so 15 a server, near the 50 ms a 20-ticks server needs (#252).
;; Memory:
;; a server's live heap is about 0.8 GB + 0.06 GB a bot, a race process's under 1 GB at 50 bots.
{:race/runners 8 ; GitHub runners; the sim race has eight more, and the other four of the twenty stay free for the suite, a fix's checks and the gym
 :race/servers 2 ; servers per runner, each its own world copy, race process and bots
 :race/landing-sets ["R1" "R2" "R3" "R4"] ; ci/gym.edn's race worlds: runner r races on set (r-1) mod 4
 :race/bots 10        ; bot slots per server, each refilled the moment its bot ends: 160 bots playing at every moment. Fortress lanes (:race/from): 15 players round three fortresses held the server tick at avg 60 to 108 ms, p95 100 to 200, against 40 to 55 and 56 to 100 on a spawn lane (lane 3, run 41218543330), so ten (a spawn race was 15, #252) (#252)
 :race/prefix "Clj_r" ; bot names: Clj_r01, Clj_r02, ... one serial per server for the job
 :race/from "fortress" ; where each bot starts: "spawn" (a forest of its landing, every stage from the wood) or "fortress" (the Nether, at the open pad 48 blocks west of its landing's fortress with :race/kit, playing only the stages from the blaze rods to :race/until: stages 17 and 18, issue #262; a failure is filed at those stages only)
 :race/kit ["minecraft:stone_pickaxe 1" "minecraft:iron_sword 1" "minecraft:iron_helmet 1"
            "minecraft:iron_chestplate 1" "minecraft:iron_leggings 1" "minecraft:cooked_beef 16"
            "minecraft:crafting_table 1" "minecraft:stick 12" "minecraft:flint_and_steel 1"
            "minecraft:bucket 1" "minecraft:water_bucket 1" "minecraft:coal 4"
            "minecraft:stone_sword 1" "minecraft:cobblestone 256" "minecraft:netherrack 64"
            "minecraft:diorite 128" "minecraft:granite 64" "minecraft:andesite 64"
            "minecraft:cobbled_deepslate 64" "minecraft:dirt 64" "minecraft:gravel 16"
            "minecraft:raw_copper 12" "minecraft:lapis_lazuli 11" "minecraft:leather 6"
            "minecraft:bone 2" "minecraft:string 3" "minecraft:oak_planks 1" "minecraft:flint 1"
            "minecraft:sand 16" "minecraft:arrow 1" "minecraft:spruce_planks 1"
            "minecraft:white_wool 2"] ; what a race bot carries to the fortress (lane audits of 2026-10-31: 36 of 36 slots used: armour in the bag, 256 to 877 cobblestone, the stones a tunnel digs, a stone pickaxe, the portal kit's bucket and flint and steel, and the odds and ends it picks up): 13 single tools and stacks, 12 stacks of stone, 11 of odds and ends, 36 slots, given when :race/from is "fortress"
 :race/until "pearls-12"   ; the target; the run plays every step up to it (plan/through): the Nether, the fortress (issue #261), seven blaze rods from its spawner (issue #262), then twelve ender pearls from endermen (issue #263). The sim race stays at blaze-rods until the model spawns the Nether's endermen
 :race/run-minutes 330     ; how long each runner plays, its slots refilled the whole time (issue #127): near GitHub's 6 h job cap, inside the job's 355 minutes with setup, the last report and the uploads
 :race/stagger-ms 3000     ; between bots joining a server
 :race/server-heap-mb 3072 ; each server's JVM: about 2.3 GB live at 25 bots
 :race/bot-heap-mb 2048}                ; each race process's JVM, its 25 bots
